cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Sema in your research or build on the pattern vocabulary,
  please cite the preprint below. The software metadata at the top of
  this file is also valid as a standalone software citation.
title: "Sema: When the Hash Is the Word"
abstract: >-
  Sema is a semantic commons that content-addresses meaning itself:
  the definition is the identifier. By deriving identifiers from the
  cryptographic hash of a pattern's definition, any divergence in
  meaning produces a distinct hash, guaranteeing that misaligned
  agents halt rather than fail silently.
authors:
